    {"type":"text","id":"pat_t","x":40,"y":1382,"width":1560,"height":30,"strokeColor":"#94a3b8","text":"[06] Calibrated Degrees of Freedom: rendering is code, so every triage starts from the same table; the one judgement is delegated to a regular expression\n[19] Scope Lock and Checkpoint Delivery: the table is the named deliverable for checkpoint A and the scope boundary for workstream D","fontSize":12,"fontFamily":3,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","roughness":0,"opacity":100,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":false,"seed":226002},
    {"type":"text","id":"missing","x":40,"y":1430,"width":1560,"height":45,"strokeColor":"#fecaca","text":"deliberately missing: suggested vs decided (a suggestion column for the pre-filled NA, the disposition column left for a human, so a gate can count human decisions)\n· all four codes: worker-node failures with no approval requirement to implement, control-plane failures pending approval to defer · one legend: render the template, not restate it","fontSize":12,"fontFamily":3,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","roughness":0,"opacity":100,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":false,"seed":226003},
    {"type":"text","id":"proto","x":40,"y":1480,"width":1560,"height":15,"strokeColor":"#94a3b8","text":"prototype: fabricated findings → the same table shape; --check counts dispositions by where they came from and runs an “every failure dispositioned” gate · Markdown only, stdout","fontSize":12,"fontFamily":3,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","roughness":0,"opacity":100,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":false,"seed":226004}
